R library in common has not been loaded.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>0 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-12-0-1/\">The Events Calendar 6.12.0.1</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:4;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:63:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:35:\"Featured Calendar: Carnegie Library\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:98:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/wordpress-calendar-examples/featured-calendar-carnegie-library/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Wed, 14 May 2025 14:00:00 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:3:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"Blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:27:\"WordPress Calendar Examples\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2547602\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:642:\"<p>In this month’s customer spotlight, we&#8217;re shining a light on the Carnegie Library and their community-focused events calendar. There’s always something happening at this library—from enriching educational workshops to engaging community events. With such a vibrant range of activities, keeping track of it all can be a challenge. That’s why they use The Events Calendar...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/wordpress-calendar-examples/featured-calendar-carnegie-library/\">Featured Calendar: Carnegie Library</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:14:\"Sarah Zuercher\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:20992:\"\n<p>In this month’s customer spotlight, we&#8217;re shining a light on the <a href=\"https://www.carnegielibrary.org/\">Carnegie Library</a> and their community-focused events calendar. There’s always something happening at this library—from enriching educational workshops to engaging community events. With such a vibrant range of activities, keeping track of it all can be a challenge. That’s why they use <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/wordpress-events-calendar/\">The Events Calendar</a> to manage events.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>This calendar is a powerful tool that helps the library promote its offerings while ensuring no one misses out on a program. We’ll get into what makes the Carnegie Library’s calendar stand out, along with some suggestions to make it even better!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-the-main-events-page\">The Main Events Page</h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-general-design\">General Design</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1564\" height=\"1600\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library main events page\" class=\"wp-image-2547603\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17.png 1564w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-293x300.png 293w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-665x680.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-83x85.png 83w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-768x786.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-1501x1536.png 1501w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-430x440.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-645x660.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-1068x1093.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-460x471.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-1074x1099.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-512x524.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-1077x1102.png 1077w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-518x530.png 518w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-600x614.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-17-500x512.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1564px) 100vw, 1564px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The general design of the Carnegie Library of Pittsburgh’s Events Calendar is both functional and consistent to the brand. Here are some key design elements we noticed on the page:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Clean and user-friendly layout:</strong> The calendar features a clean and straightforward layout, ensuring that visitors can quickly navigate and find events. The design prioritizes usability, with clear headings and descriptions, minimal distractions, and logical organization by date.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Responsive design: </strong>The calendar adapts well to all devices, whether it’s a desktop, tablet, or mobile phone. The <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/responsive-templates/\">responsive design</a> ensures that users have a seamless experience, regardless of the device they use to access the calendar.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Use of visual elements: </strong>The selected featured images and bright colors align with their brand. The featured images do a great job getting an accurate preview of each event, adding an element of interest and aiding users in quickly identifying events of interest. (<em>More on this later!)</em></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Legible typography: </strong>The typography is clear, legible, and appropriately sized per element, ensuring that event details are easy to read on any device. This helps improve the overall accessibility and ensures users can engage with the content without straining their eyes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Three featured events:</strong> They put three <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/featured-events/\">featured events</a> above the calendar. Although it’s an effective way to draw attention to events you want to showcase, the placement of these featured events could be improved, perhaps by adding more space between them and their main menu.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Colors: </strong>The Carnegie Library&#8217;s purple and yellow brand colors are present on the calendar page, which is great! However, there’s potential to use their colors more throughout the calendar. For instance, the <strong>Find Events</strong> button could be updated to match their purple or yellow brand colors.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"390\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library search bar on the main events page\" class=\"wp-image-2547604\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18.png 1600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-300x73.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-665x162.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-140x34.png 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-768x187.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-1536x374.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-430x105.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-645x157.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-1068x260.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-460x112.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-1074x262.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-512x125.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-707x172.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-600x146.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-18-500x122.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-views\">Views</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The calendar’s default layout is the list view. It is easy to navigate, making it simple for users to find exactly what they’re looking for, whether they’re interested in a book club, a youth program, or a special event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Users can switch between different calendar views, such as month, day, and week. This feature is useful for those who prefer to view the calendar in a different format.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"493\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library\'s type of calendar views on the main events page\" class=\"wp-image-2547605\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19.png 1600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-300x92.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-665x205.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-140x43.png 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-768x237.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-1536x473.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-430x132.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-645x199.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-1068x329.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-460x142.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-1074x331.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-512x158.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-707x218.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-600x185.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-19-500x154.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-navigation\">Navigation</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>One of the standout features is the ability to filter events based on categories, dates, or locations, offering personalized browsing that suits each individual’s needs. This is available with <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/wordpress-calendar-filter-bar/\">Filter Bar</a>!&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The filters available on this calendar are event type, location, age group, and virtual events. Users also have the option to hide filters and search for events using the search bar. Whether a patron is looking for an online program or a hands-on workshop at one of the library’s branches, they can find events quickly.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"493\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library\'s filters for the calendar on the main events page\" class=\"wp-image-2547606\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20.png 1600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-300x92.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-665x205.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-140x43.png 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-768x237.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-1536x473.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-430x132.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-645x199.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-1068x329.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-460x142.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-1074x331.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-512x158.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-707x218.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-600x185.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-20-500x154.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-recurring-events\">Recurring Events</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Another fantastic feature is the integration of <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/tips/how-to-add-recurring-events-to-a-wordpress-site/\">recurring events</a>. For programs that happen regularly—like weekly storytimes or monthly author readings—the calendar automatically generates recurring entries, making it effortless to showcase these ongoing events. This reduces administrative workload while ensuring consistency in the events listing. And, it makes it easier for website visitors to catch the next dates and times!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1322\" height=\"1328\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library\'s recurring events\" class=\"wp-image-2547607\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21.png 1322w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-300x300.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-665x668.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-85x85.png 85w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-768x771.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-430x432.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-645x648.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-180x180.png 180w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-270x270.png 270w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-1068x1073.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-460x462.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-1074x1079.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-512x514.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-1097x1102.png 1097w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-528x530.png 528w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-600x603.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-21-500x502.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1322px) 100vw, 1322px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-featured-images\">Featured Images</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Featured images are a consistent ratio, which we love to see! The images also are branded very well. They choose images that give a preview into the event, adding an element of interest, aiding users to know about the events at a glance. The best images help users navigate through the calendar quickly while limiting distractions. In that way, this calendar gets it right!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-kadence-image kb-image2547602_3a341c-ee size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1959\" height=\"2559\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library\'s featured images on the main events page\" class=\"kb-img wp-image-2547608\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images.png 1959w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-230x300.png 230w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-665x869.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-65x85.png 65w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-768x1003.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1176x1536.png 1176w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1568x2048.png 1568w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-430x562.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-645x843.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1068x1395.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-460x601.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1602x2093.png 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1074x1403.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-512x669.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1611x2104.png 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-844x1102.png 844w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-406x530.png 406w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-1265x1653.png 1265w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-600x784.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Carnegie-Library-Featured-Images-500x653.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1959px) 100vw, 1959px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-single-event-page\">Single Event Page</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1208\" height=\"1600\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22.png\" alt=\"Carnegie library\'s single event page, featuring the title, date, time, graphic, and description.\" class=\"wp-image-2547609\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22.png 1208w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-227x300.png 227w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-665x881.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-64x85.png 64w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-768x1017.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-1160x1536.png 1160w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-430x570.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-645x854.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-1068x1415.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-460x609.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-1074x1423.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-512x678.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-832x1102.png 832w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-400x530.png 400w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-600x795.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/image-22-500x662.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1208px) 100vw, 1208px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-clear-and-concise-information\">Clear and Concise Information</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The title and description are straightforward and easily understandable, making it clear what the program is about. This clarity lets users know exactly what to expect. Additionally, the date and time are prominently displayed, reducing confusion and making it easy to plan ahead.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-recurring-event\">Recurring Event</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>If the event is recurring, such as the one above, that is indicated above the title. Users can then view the other scheduled times for that event. Easy and convenient!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-navigation-0\">Navigation</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The page is also easy to navigate, with clear links to other events and the ability to return to the main events calendar. This makes browsing other events convenient if a visitor is looking for more activities to attend.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>All in all, it’s a well-designed, easy-to-navigate experience with clear, engaging information, all of which are key for making the event more accessible and appealing to its target audience.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-highlights-of-carnegie-library-s-calendar\">Highlights of Carnegie Library’s Calendar</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Carnegie Library of Pittsburgh’s Events Calendar is the ultimate go-to guide for everything happening at the library! My favorite parts of the calendar are:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Effective and useful event images:</strong> These branded images offer a sneak peek into the event, making them engaging and helping users spot events quickly.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Concise and clear single event pages:</strong> Each event page is clear, concise, and clutter-free—making it super easy for parents to get all the details they need.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Filter bar: </strong>The real magic comes with the ability to filter events by category, date, or location—so you can quickly find that perfect program, whether it’s a cozy storytime or a hands-on workshop.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Recurring events: </strong>Recurring events simplify browsing because you can see the future sessions on a single page.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-serving-the-community-with-an-events-calendar\">Serving the Community with an Events Calendar</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Carnegie Library’s event calendar is flowing with events. From its easy-to-navigate design and responsive layout to its vibrant event images and handy filtering options, the calendar makes it simple for users to discover and engage with library offerings. The library&#8217;s calendar is a shining example of how technology can enhance the community experience. With a few tweaks, it could be even more powerful, but as it stands, it’s already a key resource for anyone looking to explore all the wonderful things happening at the Carnegie Library! </p>\n\n\n\n<p>It’s time to join The Carnegie Library and hundreds of others in creating event calendars. If you’re a nonprofit, we also offer a <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/nonprofit-program/\">discount</a> for you! Check it out.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/wordpress-calendar-examples/featured-calendar-carnegie-library/\">Featured Calendar: Carnegie Library</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:5;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:25:\"Events Calendar Pro 7.5.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:89:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/event-calendar-pro-7-5-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 13 May 2025 14:21:51 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"Events Calendar Pro\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548472\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:561:\"<p>Summary Feature Release This version of Events Calendar Pro adds a new method to get the next Event in a Series and adds some accessibility improvements. As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✨ Features Features in this release: ✅ Fixes Bugs squashed in...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/event-calendar-pro-7-5-0/\">Events Calendar Pro 7.5.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5197:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Feature Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">This version of Events Calendar Pro adds a new method to get the next Event in a Series and adds some accessibility improvements.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-features\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Features</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>New method to get the next Event in a Series. </li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Ensure that additional field data is properly saved with the event when using the Block editor. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Prevent instances of the `_load_textdomain_just_in_time` warning by moving all language after the `init` hook</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjustments to keyboard navigation to focus on multiday and all-day events properly.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Change the wrapper div to a section tag to avoid multiple &#8216;banner&#8217; landmarks.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Added actions: `tec_events_virtual_fully_loaded`, `tec_event_automator_fully_loaded`, `tec_events_pro_fully_loaded` </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Added filters: `tec_events_qr_next_series_event_url` </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Changed views: `v2/map`, `v2/photo`, `v2/summary`, `v2/week`, `v2/week/grid-body/multiday-events-day/multiday-event/bar`, `v2/week/grid-body/multiday-events-day/multiday-event/hidden`, `v2/week/grid-body/multiday-events-day/multiday-event/hidden/link` </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include more Recurrence and Exclusion Telemetry data to improve functionality planning. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Removed actions: `tribe_log`</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>9 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>121 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/event-calendar-pro-7-5-0/\">Events Calendar Pro 7.5.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:6;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:17:\"Filter Bar 5.5.10\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:73:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/filter-bar/filter-bar-5-5-10/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 13 May 2025 14:21:49 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:10:\"Filter Bar\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548482\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:603:\"<p>Summary Maintenance Release This version of Filter Bar ensures that filtering by venue or organizer works on WPML-translated pages, along with accessibility improvements. As always, we recommend&#160;testing updates&#160;on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✅ Fixes Bugs squashed in this release: ⚙️ Tweaks Tweaks in this release: 🗣 Translations Updated...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/filter-bar/filter-bar-5-5-10/\">Filter Bar 5.5.10</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4558:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Maintenance Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">This version of Filter Bar ensures that filtering by venue or organizer works on WPML-translated pages, along with accessibility improvements.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend&nbsp;<a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a>&nbsp;on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Make sure that filtering by venue or organizer works on WPML-translated pages.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add header tags around accordion buttons to maintain semantic meaning. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add `aria-hidden=&#8221;true&#8221;` to filterbar icon for better screen reader accessibility. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improve accessibility labels for range slider. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improved accessibility of Filter Bar buttons. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Move focus to filterbar options when accordion is opened for better accessibility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tweaked the filter for Featured events for better accessibility.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Add the `tec_events_filter_additional_field_intersect` filter to allow showing all used values of additional field in Filter Bar. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ensure that Additional Field options that are removed don&#8217;t show up in Filter Bar any longer. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Added filters: `tec_events_filter_additional_field_intersect`, `tribe_filterbar_organizer_ids`, `tribe_filterbar_venue_ids`, `wpml_default_language`, `wpml_object_id`.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Changed views: `v2_1/components/events-bar/filter-button`, `v2_1/components/filter`, `v2_1/components/pill-button`, `v2_1/components/pill`, `v2_1/components/range`.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>1 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>27 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/filter-bar/filter-bar-5-5-10/\">Filter Bar 5.5.10</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:7;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:24:\"Event Tickets Plus 6.4.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:88:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets-plus/event-tickets-plus-6-4-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 13 May 2025 14:21:46 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:18:\"Event Tickets Plus\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548477\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:566:\"<p>Summary Maintenance Release This version of Event Tickets Plus includes QR-related code that has been moved from ET to Common, along with the QR code library. As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✨ Features Features in this release: ⚙️ Tweaks Tweaks in this...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets-plus/event-tickets-plus-6-4-0/\">Event Tickets Plus 6.4.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:3715:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Maintenance Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">This version of Event Tickets Plus includes QR-related code that has been moved from ET to Common, along with the QR code library.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-features\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Features</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Move QR-related code from ET to Common.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Move QR code library to Common.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Added actions: `tec_tickets_plus_fully_loaded`, `tec_tickets_wallet_plus_fully_loaded`.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Avoid multiple inits of Tribe__Tickets_Plus__Commerce__WooCommerce__Main resulting in duplicate hooks. </li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>0 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>36 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets-plus/event-tickets-plus-6-4-0/\">Event Tickets Plus 6.4.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:8;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:26:\"The Events Calendar 6.12.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:91:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-12-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 13 May 2025 14:21:44 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"The Events Calendar\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548467\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:588:\"<p>Summary Feature Release The latest update of The Events Calendar introduces the new QR Code Generation for events! Also, including improved accessibility fixes. Read more about the new QR Code Generation feature here. As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✨ Features New features...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-12-0/\">The Events Calendar 6.12.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5899:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-normal-font-size\">Feature Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The latest update of The Events Calendar introduces the new QR Code Generation for events! Also, including improved accessibility fixes.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Read more about the new QR Code Generation feature <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/qr-codes-are-here-connect-promotional-material-to-your-event-calendar-with-ease/\">here</a>.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend<a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\"> testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-features\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Features</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">New features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Add an editor block to display an event QR code.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a widget to display a QR code for an event.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add the <code>[tec_event_qr]</code> shortcode.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Generate QR Code link in the Events Admin Table.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>QR Code metabox in Events Edit screen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Support QR Codes in TEC</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"> <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Harden backend requests to enforce user capabilities.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add aria-labels to view options and aria-current to the selected view. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add aria-label to the view selector button.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add an aria label to the Add to calendar button.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Change focus to results after filtering `events/`.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Change the wrapper div to a section tag to avoid multiple &#8216;banner&#8217; landmarks.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Small tweaks to improve the accessibility of user-facing messages.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tweaked accordions so they will toggle and not submit when using keyboard navigation.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Added filters: `tec_events_qr_enabled`, `tec_events_qr_valid_screens`, `tec_events_qr_code_supported_post_types`, `tec_events_qr_code_post_types`, `tec_events_qr_code_redirection_type`, `tec_events_qr_code_modal_vars`, `tec_events_qr_code_regenerate`, `tec_events_qr_current_event_url`, `tec_events_qr_upcoming_event_url`, `tec_events_qr_specific_event_url`, `tec_events_qr_redirection_url`, `tec_events_qr_widget_options`, `tec_events_qr_widget_fields`, `tec_events_qr_next_series_event_url`, </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Added actions: `tec_events_fully_loaded` </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Changed views: `blocks/parts/subscribe-list`, `v2/components/events-bar/views`, `v2/components/events-bar/views/list/item`, `v2/components/messages`, `v2/components/subscribe-links/single-event-list`, `v2/day`, `v2/list`, `v2/month`, `v2/widgets/widget-events-qr-code`</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>61 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>145 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-12-0/\">The Events Calendar 6.12.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:9;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:20:\"Event Tickets 5.22.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:79:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets/event-tickets-5-22-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 13 May 2025 14:21:42 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Event Tickets\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548469\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:564:\"<p>Summary Maintenance Release The latest update of Event Tickets resolves an issue with Seating coupons and prevents warnings. As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✨ Features New features in this release: ✅ Fixes Bugs squashed in this release: ⚙️ Tweaks Tweaks in this...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets/event-tickets-5-22-0/\">Event Tickets 5.22.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4510:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-normal-font-size\">Maintenance Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The latest update of Event Tickets resolves an issue with Seating coupons and prevents warnings.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend<a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\"> testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-features\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Features</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">New features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Move QR-related code from ET to Common.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Move QR code library to Common</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Fix an issue when applying 100% off coupons to Seating tickets.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Prevent instances of the `_load_textdomain_just_in_time` warning by moving all language after the `init` hook</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Removed filters: `tec_tickets_qr_code_can_use`, `tribe_tickets_attendees_report_js_config` </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Added actions: `tec_tickets_fully_loaded`, `tec_tickets_promoter_fully_loaded` </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Removed actions: `tribe_tickets_plugin_loaded`</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>0 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>5 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>4 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets/event-tickets-5-22-0/\">Event Tickets 5.22.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}}}s:27:\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\";a:1:{s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:3:{s:4:\"href\";s:35:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/feed/\";s:3:\"rel\";s:4:\"self\";s:4:\"type\";s:19:\"application/rss+xml\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:44:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/syndication/\";a:2:{s:12:\"updatePeriod\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:9:\"\n	hourly	\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:15:\"updateFrequency\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"\n	1	\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}}}}}}}}s:4:\"type\";i:128;s:7:\"headers\";O:48:\"WpOrg\\Requests\\Utility\\CaseInsensitiveDictionary\":1:{s:7:\"\0*\0data\";a:15:{s:4:\"date\";s:29:\"Mon, 19 May 2025 13:30:09 GMT\";s:12:\"content-type\";s:34:\"application/rss+xml; charset=UTF-8\";s:14:\"content-length\";s:5:\"15454\";s:6:\"cf-ray\";s:20:\"9423f27efeeef1de-GRU\";s:15:\"cf-cache-status\";s:7:\"DYNAMIC\";s:13:\"cache-control\";s:12:\"max-age=3600\";s:16:\"content-encoding\";s:4:\"gzip\";s:7:\"expires\";s:29:\"Mon, 19 May 2025 14:30:09 GMT\";s:13:\"last-modified\";s:29:\"Fri, 16 May 2025 16:48:08 GMT\";s:4:\"link\";s:117:\"<https://theeventscalendar.com/wp-json/>; rel=\"https://api.w.org/\", <https://theeventscalendar.com/>; rel=\"canonical\"\";s:4:\"vary\";s:15:\"Accept-Encoding\";s:9:\"x-nocache\";s:1:\"1\";s:13:\"server-timing\";s:28:\"cfCacheStatus;desc=\"DYNAMIC\"\";s:6:\"server\";s:10:\"cloudflare\";s:7:\"alt-svc\";s:19:\"h3=\":443\"; ma=86400\";}}s:5:\"build\";s:14:\"20211220193300\";}', 'no');
