ermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:1235:\"<img width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https://iotvnaw69daj.i.optimole.com/cb:mLvy.66914/w:150/h:150/q:mauto/rt:fill/g:ce/f:best/https://wpshout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Thoughts-on-the-Ghibli-AI-Trend.png\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image\" alt=\"Thoughts on the Ghibli AI Trend\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://iotvnaw69daj.i.optimole.com/cb:mLvy.66914/w:150/h:150/q:mauto/rt:fill/g:ce/f:best/https://wpshout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Thoughts-on-the-Ghibli-AI-Trend.png 150w, https://iotvnaw69daj.i.optimole.com/cb:mLvy.66914/w:150/h:150/q:mauto/rt:fill/g:ce/f:best/dpr:2/https://wpshout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Thoughts-on-the-Ghibli-AI-Trend.png 2x\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" />Back in 2018 I spent some time in the city of Mitaka - which happens to be where the Ghibli Museum is located. I walked by it several times a week and have fond memories from there. When the internet became flooded with Ghibli style art last week after OpenAI released their newest AI image generator, my reaction was probably more visceral than most people\'s. After spending some time Ghibli-ficating myself, reading others\' opinions, and having a few days to reflect on it all, here are my thoughts.\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:14:\"Martin Dubovic\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:36:\"http://wellformedweb.org/CommentAPI/\";a:1:{s:10:\"commentRss\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:41:\"https://wpshout.com/ghibli-ai-trend/feed/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";